                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So the best way I can think to describe this is its a precision platrformer where you play as Sonic the Hedgehog forever curled into a ball and your only enemies are the laws of physics and inertia. \n\nI got sick of it during level 2 but from what I played, there are checkpoints after each small group of obstacles that usually just involve platforming with no real control. It would be a fun game, but it just doesn't feel good to play. It's like playing one of those old wooden labyrinth games from way back in the day, but way harder. I tried with keyboard and controller, and neither left me with the impression that I was in \"control.\" So any time I passed a challenge, it felt mostly due to luck rather than any real skill.\n\nIf you're into precision platformers that are more on the relaxed side, I would say give it a shot, but only if you want to challenge physics as a ball. Cuz honestly, it's not very fun.\n\nIt looks like it's only about 6 levels, but the levels are rather long.\n\nOh, and it always launched at the lowest resolution setting each time I started the game, and to switch it is a tedious process as it's very slow in moving through all the resolutions up to the one I needed. That alone doesn't make this game worth playing.",
